WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.810
So who starts the new strand?

00:00:02.437 --> 00:00:03.343
Meet primase.

00:00:03.877 --> 00:00:05.491
Primase can start from scratch.

00:00:06.118 --> 00:00:07.348
It lays down a short piece of

00:00:07.453 --> 00:00:08.695
RNA called a primer.

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.193
Like the first brick the rest stack

00:00:10.262 --> 00:00:10.587
on.

00:00:11.435 --> 00:00:13.908
Now DNA polymerase has a 3-prime end.

00:00:14.303 --> 00:00:16.160
It adds DNA right onto the primer.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.248
Primase makes a short RNA primer, and

00:00:19.295 --> 00:00:20.920
DNA polymerase builds onto it.

00:00:21.547 --> 00:00:22.719
Swipe for the recap.
